{
  "case_id": "2012-12-135",
  "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nSETH P. WAXMAN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Petitioner.\nERIC D. KATZ, ESQ., Roseland, New Jersey; on behalf of Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But -- about the parties never considering it, when this case was in the New Jersey courts, Oxford explained -- this is in the red brief at page 27 that's quoting Oxford's counsel then, that \"the arbitrator has the power to ascertain whether the parties contemplated class arbitration in their agreements.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: That's my question. Did you never -- you never argued that it was beyond the power of the arbitrator to decide this question, did you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So your rule is that although we must defer to an arbitrator's interpretation of the contract, in this case, there is an exception because?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You're -- you're saying that this is off the wall. That's your -- to put it in -- in Justice Ginsburg's terms, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Waxman, could I just ask you what you think the standard is under 10(a)(4) because my understanding of the standard was that a court had to find that an arbitrator was exceeding his powers, was acting outside the scope of his authority --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Out of curiosity, Mr. Waxman, in a case like this, how is the arbitrator paid? Is the arbitrator paid by the hour or a flat fee?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Waxman, how wrong does an arbitrator's decision have to be to become an issue of law? Meaning -- because that's the rule you're proposing. I used to think that exceeding your powers was deciding an issue the parties hadn't agreed to arbitrate, but here you've conceded that you gave the issue to the arbitrator. So he hasn't exceeded his power to construe the contract with respect to this dispute, do you agree with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Oxford",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Oxford cannot satisfy either of those standards here. Oxford does not dispute that the arbitrator interpreted the contract. Oxford's sole dispute here or challenge is that the -- that the arbitrator interpreted the contract incorrectly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Oxford",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Oxford has always maintained that it was the arbitrator's decision to make, and in 2010, even after Stolt-Nielsen, came back to the arbitrator and asked the arbitrator to reconsider his opinion from 2003."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I ask you a question on something a little bit different? Did the arbitrator have -- how many parties were there to this agreement? There is Oxford on one side and how many doctors on the other side?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Oxford",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Oxford argued that the class action should go into arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How can they opt out if they've agreed to class arbitration?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Katz",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATZ: Well, they can opt out of the class and pursue, if they wanted to at that point, an individual arbitration if that's what they chose to do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, presumably they could opt out, but did they agree to be bound by this unless they opted out? That's not the usual way people are bound by litigations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: It would be impossible because you could never get in advance -- they find out that by getting notice and then they decide whether they want to stay with it or opt out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Oxford",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it was Oxford's argument that everything including the class action go into arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Waxman",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8e26764410c00fea29807778d5de4abd2e1ee53733746b0320d7fba8df313fc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8e26764410c-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the AAA class arbitration rules were adopted after this Court's decision in Bazzle, which left open the possibility, a possibility that the arbitrator in this case said was surprising because the arbitrator said quite correctly that everyone expected that in Bazzle this Court would say there's no such thing as class arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-12-135",
      "confidence": 0.0,
